From 8d8cb579e4ba340a4bd943daca58dffa47aa2559 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:25:19 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ARM: dts: qcom: add separate Madai CPU qualification target

Retain the current ordinary board charging, USB, NFC and other device
definitions. Add only the L2/S2 CPU foundation and complete eight-byte
CPU calibration row. Its ordinary four CPU rates and absent CPR consumer
remain unchanged. A separate explicit qualification target describes all
fourteen canonical rates and their matching domain links.

Register the additional target in the existing complete LTS board list.
The ordinary board retains the shared APC setup and eight-byte CPU raw
cell; the separate target describes the calibrated domain/OPP contract.
Sixteen baseline and seventeen candidate family DTBs build. The other
15 board binaries remain byte-identical. Both Madai targets pass their
selected schema checks and each repeat three inherited DTC warnings;
the total 65-to-68 increase adds no distinct warning. The experimental
target does not fulfill the final normal-target or physical acceptance.

Backport as part of the initial maintained-6.18.63 CPU stack. The complete
series passes 45 selected host test methods. Standalone executables use
ASan, UBSan and normal LeakSanitizer; ctypes numerical oracles are
explicitly unsanitized. Twenty selected objects compile with the feature
enabled and disabled on ARM, ARM64 and ARM64 RT (120 objects), W=1 and
nonpermissive CFI, with no diagnostics. ARM32 RT is unsupported.

Original author/date and source notices are preserved. Codex prepared
this local backport and verification. Original scoped source provenance
remains recorded in the review evidence. Human review and DCO remain
pending; no phone, publication or maintainer action has occurred.

Backported from commit 57b4bd9ec2db78022e93be3c5bef3e9e25833f12 ("ARM: dts:
qcom: add separate Madai CPU qualification target")
